# NDR MIXED-RULE BUNDLE vehicle (requirement R8, the richer half).
#
# Phase 1 ships R8's FALLBACK: a bundle must be rule-uniform, so the
# bundler splits a mixed one into rule-uniform parts, loudly.  That is
# correct and never silently drops a constraint — the cost is that a bus
# whose bits genuinely deserve different treatment routes as SEVERAL
# bundles, losing the shared trunk and the shared shields.
#
# This vehicle is the case that pays that cost.  `mix_` is ONE 8-bit bus
# between one block pair whose bits carry THREE rules by prefix:
#
#   mix_hi_[0..1]  hi2x   width x2 shield bus net GND   (2 slots/bit)
#   mix_md_[0..3]  md15   width x1.5 spacing x1.5       (2 slots + 1 guard)
#   mix_lo_[0..1]  (none) default                       (1 slot/bit)
#
# TODAY: three bundles, three trunks, and hi2x's flanking shields wrap only
# its own two bits.  The split report names the parts.
#
# UNDER R8's richer position: ONE bundle, one trunk, and the group demand
# is the sum of the MEMBERS' footprints with each gap priced by the pair it
# separates — shared shields and interior spacing counted ONCE at the group
# level, exactly as `ndr_group_demand` already does for a uniform group.
# That is the generalization: the conversion takes a MEMBER LIST rather
# than (spec, nbits), and every consumer follows.
#
# What the vehicle must show either way:
#   * the demand is the SUM over members, not nbits x one spec — an 8-bit
#     mixed group is not 8 x anything;
#   * a shield between two members of DIFFERENT rules is counted once, not
#     once per rule (the group-level property R4 already guarantees within
#     a uniform group);
#   * splitting CHANGES the shield count — a flanked group cut in two pays
#     four end shields where the whole paid two — and the split report
#     surfaces that delta rather than leaving it implicit (R8's explicit
#     requirement);
#   * check_design stays clean under both positions, and the R9 arrangement
#     walk still reads the run role-by-role — with a per-member layout, not
#     a single-spec one.
#
# `same_` is the control: an 8-bit bus over the same block pair under ONE
# rule, so the mixed group's demand can be read against a uniform one of
# equal width rather than against a hand-computed number.
#
# STATUS: runs TODAY, exercising the fallback (three parts, split reported).
# It is committed in that state deliberately — it is the before/after
# measurement for the richer position, and the WL cost of splitting is
# exactly what the change has to justify.

add_block blkA 0   0    200 400
add_block blkB 800 0    1000 400
add_block blkC 0   500  200 900
add_block blkD 800 500  1000 900

# One bus, three rule classes by prefix.
add_bus mix_hi_[2] blkA.p blkB.q
add_bus mix_md_[4] blkA.p blkB.q
add_bus mix_lo_[2] blkA.p blkB.q

# Control: same width, one rule, its own block pair.
add_bus same_[8] blkC.p blkD.q

def_layer 3 M3 H 20
def_layer 4 M4 V 20
def_layer 5 M5 H TOP 20
def_layer 6 M6 V TOP 20

def_ndr hi2x width x2 shield bus net GND
def_ndr md15 width x1.5 spacing x1.5
set_ndr mix_hi_ hi2x
set_ndr mix_md_ md15
# mix_lo_ deliberately unscoped — a DEFAULT member inside the mixed group.
set_ndr same_ hi2x

run_bundler STRICT --dump
dump_ndr

generate_topologies
set_track_pitch 3
run_planner 1

def_track_pattern 3 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 4 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 5 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1
def_track_pattern 6 0 VDD 2 1 (_ 1 1)x12 GND 2 1

run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
dump_ndr
check_design
report_wirelength
